3.2. SAE levels

Fully automated vehicles are on the rise (Autonomous Vehicles Market to Surpass USD 2324.5 Billion by 2030 on Account of Rising Consumer Demand and Increasing R&D Investments | Research by SNS Insider, 2023). Whilst current commercial automated vehicles are very limited and typically SAE level 2 (user supervises and fallback ready) (International, S, SAE J 3016 - Taxonomy and Definitions for Terms Related to Driving Automation Systems for On-Road Motor Vehicles, Citation 2023 ). A very limited number of systems are currently on track to achieve SAE Level 3 (fallback ready) (International, S, SAE J 3016 - Taxonomy and Definitions for Terms Related to Driving Automation Systems for On-Road Motor Vehicles, Citation 2023 ); Table 1 summarises the information from SAE International J3016 regarding the different levels of automation.

